cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, or cite the values it establishes, please cite the archived version below."
title: "RadoRecords: SAT witnesses and DRAT-certified refutations for the 2-color Rado numbers"
abstract: >-
  Computational evidence for terms a(31)-a(60) of OEIS A250026, the 2-color Rado
  numbers of x_1^2 + x_2^2 + ... + x_n^2 = z^2. Lower bounds are explicit
  colorings checked by a standard-library-only program that never invokes a
  solver; upper bounds are SAT refutations certified with drat-trim, computed
  under two independent encodings that must agree at every instance.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Leo Y.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-1145-7969"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Leo-Y-Zhang/RadoRecords"
license-url: "https://github.com/Leo-Y-Zhang/RadoRecords/blob/main/LICENSE"
